cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this corpus, please cite it as below."
title: "WebInject2026: A Leakage-Audited Corpus for Web Injection Detection"
version: 4.4.0
date-released: 2026-08-08
type: dataset
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/anishc23/webinject2026"
abstract: >-
  A contemporary, leakage-audited corpus for web-application injection-attack
  detection: 61,400 labelled HTTP requests across three deliberately vulnerable
  practice applications and fourteen attack families, with fixed
  payload-disjoint and template-disjoint splits and an automated 30-check
  quality gate that fails the build if a known shortcut or label leak reappears.
keywords:
  - web application security
  - injection attacks
  - intrusion detection
  - dataset
  - data leakage
